Day 1 – Harbour Internship
Session: Git vs GitHub & Creating a README

On Day 1 of my Harbour internship, I learned the difference between Git and GitHub and understood how they are used in software development. The session covered the basics of version control, Git repositories, commits, and how GitHub helps in storing and collaborating on code online.

I also learned how to create and manage a README.md file for a GitHub repository, including adding project information and documentation. This session helped me understand the importance of version control and maintaining a well-documented project repository.
